---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import FinalCTA from '@/components/FinalCTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Architecting Amazon Music's Livestream Strategy"
  description=""
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 1: HERO
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div>
      <span class="section-tag">Case Study</span>
      <h1>Architecting Amazon Music's Livestream Strategy</h1>
      <p class="hero-desc">
        Amazon Music had access to the biggest artists and cultural moments in music — but livestreams were treated as isolated activations. I architected the marketing and growth strategy that transformed livestreams into a scalable audience growth engine, powering flagship programming like Amazon Music Live and landmark events like Kendrick Lamar's The Pop Out.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-meta">
        <div class="hero-meta-item">
          <span class="hero-meta-label">Company</span>
          <span class="hero-meta-value">Amazon Music</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-meta-item">
          <span class="hero-meta-label">Industry</span>
          <span class="hero-meta-value">Entertainment / Livestreaming</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-meta-item">
          <span class="hero-meta-label">Scope</span>
          <span class="hero-meta-value">Global</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-meta-item">
          <span class="hero-meta-label">Focus</span>
          <span class="hero-meta-value">Growth Strategy &amp; Live Programming</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-image" style="padding:0; background:none; border:none;">
          <img src="https://static.wixstatic.com/media/d84514_ffa2dc6ea5ea445bb9a5e54c917e2ef8~mv2.png" alt="Amazon Music Live marketing" style="width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; border-radius:var(--radius);" />
        </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 2: RESULTS STRIP
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="results-strip">
  <div class="results-strip-inner">
    <div class="result-stat">
      <div class="result-number">+31%</div>
      <div class="result-label">Customer Growth</div>
    </div>
    <div class="result-stat">
      <div class="result-number">+39%</div>
      <div class="result-label">Revenue Growth</div>
    </div>
    <div class="result-stat">
      <div class="result-number">+3.7pt</div>
      <div class="result-label">Brand Favorability Lift</div>
    </div>
    <div class="result-stat">
      <div class="result-number">Flagship</div>
      <div class="result-label">Live Performance Series</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 3: THE SITUATION
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="content-section">
  <span class="section-tag">The Situation</span>
  <h2>Cultural Moments Were Being Wasted as One-Off Activations</h2>
  <p>
    Amazon Music had access to some of the biggest artists, festivals, and cultural moments in music. However, these events were historically treated as isolated marketing activations rather than a unified strategy for audience growth. Fan behavior was shifting toward livestreaming, yet the opportunity remained unrealized.
  </p>
  <div class="challenge-grid">
    <ul class="challenge-points">
      <li class="challenge-point">
        <div class="challenge-icon">1</div>
        <div class="challenge-text">
          <strong>Livestreams were treated as isolated promotions.</strong> Major cultural moments — festivals, album drops, artist performances — generated attention but were not connected to a repeatable growth framework.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="challenge-point">
        <div class="challenge-icon">2</div>
        <div class="challenge-text">
          <strong>Fan behavior was shifting to live digital experiences.</strong> Younger audiences were consuming culture through platforms like Twitch and live digital events, but Amazon Music hadn't built a strategy for this shift.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="challenge-point">
        <div class="challenge-icon">3</div>
        <div class="challenge-text">
          <strong>Amazon's ecosystem was a unique but unrealized advantage.</strong> Twitch, Prime Video, and Amazon Music created a powerful distribution network — but no unified strategy connected them for live programming.
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="challenge-point">
        <div class="challenge-icon">4</div>
        <div class="challenge-text">
          <strong>No repeatable operating model existed.</strong> Each event required building from scratch rather than operating from a scalable playbook for live music programming.
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="challenge-callout">
      <span class="section-tag">The Mandate</span>
      <blockquote>
        Transform livestreams from one-off promotional moments into a scalable audience growth engine — connecting artists, fans, and Amazon's media ecosystem.
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 4: THE APPROACH
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="approach-bg">
  <div class="content-section">
    <span class="section-tag">The Approach</span>
    <h2>Culture-First Programming Meets Ecosystem Amplification</h2>
    <p>
      I developed the strategic framework that positioned livestreams as a core pillar of Amazon Music's growth strategy. The model focused on three key principles: culture-first programming, ecosystem amplification across Amazon platforms, and marketing designed for discovery.
    </p>
    <div class="approach-phases">
      <div class="phase-card">
        <div class="phase-number">01</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Culture-First Programming</div>
        <div class="phase-desc">
          Prioritized events that fans already cared about — festivals, artist moments, and major cultural conversations. Amazon Music participated in moments with existing momentum rather than trying to manufacture interest.
        </div>
        <div class="phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="phase-tool">Go-to-Market Strategy →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phase-card">
        <div class="phase-number">02</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Ecosystem Amplification</div>
        <div class="phase-desc">
          Connected multiple Amazon platforms into a unified distribution strategy. Livestreams were distributed across Twitch and Prime Video while driving listeners back into Amazon Music for deeper catalog engagement.
        </div>
        <div class="phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/integrated-marketing" class="phase-tool">Integrated Marketing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phase-card">
        <div class="phase-number">03</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Marketing Designed for Discovery</div>
        <div class="phase-desc">
          Each livestream was treated as a growth event. Campaigns combined paid media, artist co-marketing, owned Amazon channels, and PR to maximize reach and bring new audiences into the ecosystem.
        </div>
        <div class="phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/growth-marketing" class="phase-tool">Growth &amp; Lifecycle Marketing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phase-card">
        <div class="phase-number">04</div>
        <div class="phase-title">Repeatable Operating Model</div>
        <div class="phase-desc">
          Formalized the approach into a scalable playbook that worked across festivals, album launches, cultural events, and original programming — turning individual activations into an ongoing growth engine.
        </div>
        <div class="phase-tools">
          <a href="/services/content-creator-marketing" class="phase-tool">Content &amp; Creator Marketing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 5: VISUAL GALLERY
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 6: BEFORE / AFTER
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="before-after">
  <div class="before-after-inner">
    <span class="section-tag">Transformation</span>
    <h2>Before &amp; After the Livestream Strategy</h2>
    <div class="ba-grid">
      <div class="ba-column ba-before">
        <div class="ba-label">Before</div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">Livestreams treated as isolated one-off marketing activations</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">No unified strategy connecting Twitch, Prime Video, and Amazon Music</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">Cultural moments generated attention but not measurable growth</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">Each event required building marketing programs from scratch</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ba-column ba-after">
        <div class="ba-label">After</div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">Livestreams operating as a scalable, repeatable audience growth engine</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">Unified ecosystem strategy distributing content across all Amazon platforms</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">31% customer growth and 39% revenue growth from live programming</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ba-item">
          <div class="ba-bullet"></div>
          <div class="ba-item-text">Amazon Music Live established as a flagship series with global artists</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 7: RESULTS DEEP DIVE
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="results-section">
  <div class="results-inner">
    <span class="section-tag">Results</span>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif; font-size:clamp(28px,3.5vw,40px); text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--dark); margin-bottom:8px;">
      The Numbers Tell the Story
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px; color:rgba(33,54,33,0.65); max-width:600px;">
      A unified livestream strategy that turned cultural moments into one of Amazon Music's most powerful audience engagement channels.
    </p>
    <div class="results-grid">
      <div class="result-card">
        <div class="result-card-metric">+31%</div>
        <div class="result-card-label">Customer Growth</div>
        <div class="result-card-desc">
          Livestream programming drove significant customer acquisition, turning cultural music moments into measurable platform growth through integrated campaigns.
        </div>
        <div class="result-card-bar"><div class="result-card-bar-fill" style="width:85%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="result-card">
        <div class="result-card-metric">+39%</div>
        <div class="result-card-label">Revenue Growth</div>
        <div class="result-card-desc">
          The livestream strategy directly contributed to revenue growth by converting live event audiences into engaged Amazon Music subscribers and listeners.
        </div>
        <div class="result-card-bar"><div class="result-card-bar-fill" style="width:90%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="result-card">
        <div class="result-card-metric">+3.7pt</div>
        <div class="result-card-label">Brand Favorability Increase</div>
        <div class="result-card-desc">
          Live programming featuring top-tier artists elevated Amazon Music's brand perception, strengthening its position in the competitive streaming landscape.
        </div>
        <div class="result-card-bar"><div class="result-card-bar-fill" style="width:75%"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="result-card">
        <div class="result-card-metric">Flagship</div>
        <div class="result-card-label">Amazon Music Live Series</div>
        <div class="result-card-desc">
          Established Amazon Music Live as a premier live performance series featuring global artists including Megan Thee Stallion, Jelly Roll, Garth Brooks, and Snoop Dogg.
        </div>
        <div class="result-card-bar"><div class="result-card-bar-fill" style="width:95%"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 8: IMPACT
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="impact-section">
  <span class="section-tag">Impact</span>
  <h2>From One-Off Events to a Growth Engine</h2>
  <p>
    By architecting a unified strategy for livestream programming, Amazon Music transformed live events from isolated promotional moments into a scalable audience growth engine. The approach connected artists, fans, and Amazon's broader media ecosystem — establishing livestreams as one of the company's most powerful tools for cultural relevance, discovery, and fan engagement.
  </p>
  <p>
    The strategy became the blueprint for Amazon Music's live programming, powering everything from weekly artist performances to culturally significant moments like Kendrick Lamar's The Pop Out — one of the most watched music livestream events of the year.
  </p>
  <div class="impact-callout">
    <div class="impact-icon">🎤</div>
    <div class="impact-text">
      Amazon Music's livestream strategy turned cultural moments into a scalable growth engine — connecting artists, fans, and Amazon's ecosystem to drive 31% customer growth and establish the platform as a destination for live music.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 9: SERVICES USED
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="services-used">
  <span class="section-tag">Capabilities Applied</span>
  <h2 style="font-family:'Anton',sans-serif; font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px); text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--dark); margin-bottom:8px;">
    What This Took
  </h2>
  <div class="services-pills">
    <a href="/services/go-to-market" class="service-pill">Go-to-Market Strategy</a>
    <a href="/services/integrated-marketing" class="service-pill">Integrated Marketing</a>
    <a href="/services/content-creator-marketing" class="service-pill">Content &amp; Creator Marketing</a>
    <a href="/services/growth-marketing" class="service-pill">Growth &amp; Lifecycle Marketing</a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 10: CTA
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<FinalCTA />

<div class="lightbox-overlay" id="heroLightbox" onclick="this.classList.remove('active')">
  <span class="lightbox-close">&times;</span>
  <img id="lightboxImg" src="" alt="" />
</div>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
.section-tag {
    font-family: 'Satoshi', sans-serif;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2.5px;
    color: var(--dark);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    display: block;
}
.hero {
    background: var(--dark);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 152px 24px 60px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
}
.hero-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-w);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
}
.hero .section-tag { color: var(--accent); }
.hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
}
.hero-desc {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: rgba(239,234,211,0.8);
    max-width: 500px;
        margin-left: auto;
        margin-right: auto;
        margin-bottom: 28px;
    line-height: 1.7;
}
.hero-meta { display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }
.hero-meta-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
.hero-meta-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    color: var(--tan);
    font-weight: 700;
}
.hero-meta-value { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--cream); }
.hero-image {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgba(239,234,211,0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(239,234,211,0.12);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--tan);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
}
.results-strip { background: var(--accent); padding: 40px 24px; }
.results-strip-inner {
    max-width: var(--max-w);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
    text-align: center;
}
.result-number {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 44px);
    color: var(--dark);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.result-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    color: rgba(33,54,33,0.7);
}
.content-section {
    padding: 72px 24px;
    max-width: var(--max-w);
    margin: 0 auto;
}
.content-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dark);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    line-height: 1.1;
}
.content-section p {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: rgba(33,54,33,0.75);
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
}
.challenge-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 32px;
}
.challenge-points {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
}
.challenge-point { display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start; }
.challenge-icon {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--dark);
    color: var(--accent);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-weight: 700;
}
.challenge-text { font-size: 15px; color: var(--dark); line-height: 1.6; }
.challenge-text strong { font-weight: 700; }
.challenge-callout {
    background: var(--dark);
    color: var(--cream);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 32px;
}
.challenge-callout .section-tag { color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 16px; }
.challenge-callout blockquote {
    font-size: 18px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: rgba(239,234,211,0.9);
}
.challenge-callout cite {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--tan);
    font-weight: 600;
}
.approach-bg { background: var(--dark); padding: 72px 24px; }
.approach-bg .content-section { padding: 0; max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; }
.approach-bg .section-tag { color: var(--accent); }
.approach-bg h2 { color: var(--cream); }
.approach-bg p { color: rgba(239,234,211,0.7); }
.approach-phases {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
    margin-top: 40px;
}
.phase-card {
    background: rgba(239,234,211,0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(239,234,211,0.1);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 28px;
    transition: border-color 0.3s;
}
.phase-card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
.phase-number {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: 36px;
    color: var(--accent);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.phase-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--cream); margin-bottom: 8px; }
.phase-desc { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(239,234,211,0.6); line-height: 1.6; }
.phase-tools { margin-top: 14px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; }
.phase-tool {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background: rgba(165,219,93,0.12);
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.3s, color 0.3s;
    display: inline-block;
}
a.phase-tool:hover { background: var(--accent); color: var(--dark); }
.gallery-section {
    padding: 72px 24px;
    max-width: var(--max-w);
    margin: 0 auto;
}
.gallery-item {
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--dark);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: var(--tan);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid rgba(33,54,33,0.1);
    position: relative;
}
.before-after { background: var(--dark); padding: 72px 24px; }
.before-after-inner { max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; }
.before-after .section-tag { color: var(--accent); }
.before-after h2 {
    color: var(--cream);
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(28px,3.5vw,40px);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
}
.ba-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; }
.ba-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
}
.ba-before .ba-label { color: var(--tan); border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(185,169,143,0.3); }
.ba-after .ba-label { color: var(--accent); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); }
.ba-item { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.ba-bullet { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; margin-top: 6px; flex-shrink: 0; }
.ba-before .ba-bullet { background: var(--tan); opacity: 0.5; }
.ba-after .ba-bullet { background: var(--accent); }
.ba-item-text { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }
.ba-before .ba-item-text { color: rgba(239,234,211,0.5); }
.ba-after .ba-item-text { color: rgba(239,234,211,0.85); }
.results-section { background: var(--light-cream); padding: 72px 24px; }
.results-inner { max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; }
.results-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 40px;
}
.result-card {
    background: white;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 32px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(185,169,143,0.2);
}
.result-card-metric {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: 40px;
    color: var(--dark);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.result-card-label {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    color: var(--tan);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
}
.result-card-desc { font-size: 14px; color: rgba(33,54,33,0.65); line-height: 1.6; }
.result-card-bar {
    height: 4px;
    background: rgba(33,54,33,0.06);
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-top: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
}
.result-card-bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--accent);
    border-radius: 2px;
    transition: width 1s ease;
}
.impact-section { padding: 72px 24px; max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; }
.impact-section h2 {
    font-family: 'Anton', sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--dark);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    line-height: 1.1;
